@page "/wiki"
@page "/wiki/civics"
@page "/wiki/civics/{Key}"

@*
    The civics, as a page to read.

    Two addresses, because /wiki is what somebody types and a wiki with two sections needs one of
    them to be the way in. The civics are the larger shelf and the one a reader is likelier to have
    a name in mind from, so they are it.

    The page itself is a title and a shelf. Everything else is in WikiShelf, which the origins page
    is the same call to with a different word - they are the same record in the data, and the only
    reason they are two pages is that they are two different things to a player.

    The second address is one entry of the shelf. It shows the same page and picks that one out, so a
    reader who found the thing they came for can send somebody straight to it rather than to a list
    with an instruction to scroll.
*@

<PageTitle>Civics - Stellaris Empire Manager</PageTitle>

<WikiSection Kind="WikiKind.Civics" Focus="@Key" />

@code {
    /// <summary>The entry the address names, where it names one.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Key { get; set; }
}
